---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { site } from '../data/site'

const licenseUrl = `${site.github}/blob/main/LICENSE`
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Legal — Argus"
  description="Legal and third-party notices for Argus: its relationship to GitHub and OpenCode, trademark notices, and license terms."
>
  <div class="container-site py-12">
    <article class="prose">
      <header class="mb-8 not-prose">
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-fg">Legal &amp; Third-Party Notices</h1>
        <p class="mt-2 text-fg-muted">
          How Argus relates to GitHub and OpenCode, trademark notices, and license terms.
        </p>
      </header>

      <h2>Argus Project</h2>
      <p>
        Argus is an open source project released under the{' '}
        <a href={licenseUrl}>MIT License</a>, crafted and maintained by{' '}
        <a href={site.creatorUrl}>CGArtLab</a>. The source code is available at{' '}
        <a href={site.github}>github.com/cgartlab/argus</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Independent Project</h2>
      <p>
        Argus is an independent project. It is <strong>not</strong> affiliated with, sponsored
        by, or endorsed by <strong>GitHub, Inc.</strong> or{' '}
        <strong>Anomaly Innovations, Inc. (OpenCode)</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Argus is <em>built on</em> GitHub's App and Actions infrastructure and uses the OpenCode
        CLI to run reviews. Using these services does not imply any official association with,
        or endorsement by, their owners.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-Party Trademarks</h2>
      <h3>GitHub</h3>
      <p>
        GitHub, the GitHub logo, GitHub Actions, and GitHub Apps are trademarks or registered
        trademarks of <a href="https://github.com">GitHub, Inc.</a> Argus operates as the
        "argus-flash" GitHub App and uses GitHub Actions, but is not affiliated with GitHub, Inc.
      </p>
      <h3>OpenCode</h3>
      <p>
        OpenCode is a project of{' '}
        <a href="https://anoma.ly">Anomaly Innovations, Inc.</a> (opencode.ai), with source code
        available at{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode">github.com/anomalyco/opencode</a>. Argus
        uses the OpenCode CLI to run code reviews. We acknowledge OpenCode's{' '}
        <a href="https://opencode.ai/brand">brand guidelines</a> and its{' '}
        <a href="https://opencode.ai/legal/terms-of-service">Terms of Use</a>. OpenCode is a
        trademark of Anomaly Innovations, Inc.
      </p>
      <p>
        All other trademarks, service marks, and company names are the property of their
        respective owners.
      </p>

      <h2>How Argus Uses Third-Party Services</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>GitHub App (argus-flash):</strong> authenticates with the GitHub API and posts
          review comments on pull requests.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>GitHub Actions:</strong> runs the review workflow that invokes the Argus
          composite action on each pull request.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>OpenCode CLI:</strong> executes the actual AI review against Argus rules
          (<code>AGENTS.md</code> + <code>SKILL.md</code>).
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These services are used in compliance with their respective terms. Argus does not
        redistribute OpenCode source code — it invokes the OpenCode CLI at runtime. Per
        OpenCode's Terms of Use, OpenCode retains all right, title and interest in its Services,
        and its open source software remains subject to the license terms on the applicable
        repository.
      </p>

      <h2>No Warranty</h2>
      <p>
        Argus is provided "as-is" under the MIT License, without warranty of any kind, express or
        implied. See the <a href={licenseUrl}>LICENSE</a> file for the full license text.
      </p>

      <p class="not-prose mt-10 border-t border-border pt-4 text-sm text-fg-muted">
        Last updated: 2026-08-31 ·{' '}
        <a href={licenseUrl} class="no-underline text-fg-muted hover:text-fg">LICENSE</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>